    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "After a storm damages your roof, ensure your immediate safety by staying off the roof, checking your property from the ground for hazards like downed power lines, documenting all visible interior and exterior damage with photos, and temporarily tarping leaks or calling a professional roofer.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Watch this short video to learn how to spot signs of storm damage from a safe distance:",
        "video": {
          "link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bBFCExBd2aw&t=21",
          "thumbnail": "https://serpapi.com/images/i/R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAP_______yH5BAEKAAEALAAAAAABAAEAAAICTAEAOw.gif"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Immediate Safety and Protection"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Check for hazards: Look for downed power lines or structural dangers before stepping outside."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Stay off the roof:\nWet surfaces and compromised decking make climbing dangerous."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Stop active leaks: Place buckets under leaks and move valuables out of harm's way."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cover exposed areas:\nUse a heavy-duty waterproof tarp secured with wooden boards if you have open holes or missing sections."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          4
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Documentation and Professional Help"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Take photos: Snap clear pictures of missing shingles, dented gutters, fallen branches, and indoor ceiling stains."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Call an expert:\nSchedule an inspection with a reputable local roofing professional to evaluate hidden or subtle damage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "File a claim: As noted by a consensus on , contact your homeowner's insurance carrier right away to start a claim if significant damage is confirmed.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "link": "https://www.quora.com/What-should-I-do-immediately-after-storm-damage-to-my-roof"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          5
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you want, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of storm\noccurred (hail, high winds, heavy rain)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What visible damage you can see from the ground"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you prepare for the next steps or understand what to expect during an insurance claim."
      }
